# *** THESE PATTERNS LIVE HERE, NOT IN THE WALK DIRECTORIES, AND THAT IS THE FIX
# FOR A NEAR-MISS ON A PUBLIC REPO. ***
#
# Each browser walk shipped its own `.gitignore` next to its scratch dirs. That
# works until you switch branches: once `scripts/modal-walk/.gitignore` was
# COMMITTED on one branch, checking out a branch that predates it DELETED the
# ignore file while leaving the untracked Chrome profiles on disk — so the next
# `git add -A web-ui/scripts` swept in 980 files containing absolute
# `/Users/<name>/...` paths, and pushed them to a public repository.
#
# `test_no_private_data_in_tracked_files.py` caught it and failed CI, which is the
# only reason it is not still there. A per-directory ignore protects a directory
# only while the branch you are on knows about it; these patterns are repo-wide.
scripts/*/.chrome-profile*/
scripts/*/.pages/
scripts/*/captured/
e2e/.auth/
test-results/
playwright-report/
